IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `hda-types`
IMPORT `hda-flats`
IMPORT `hda-upgrading-board`
IMPORT `hda-goal`

-- Housing and Development Act 1959 — THE ENCODER'S TESTS.
-- Expected values worked by hand from ../source/HDA1959.txt.

§ `Tests`

§§ `Helpers`

GIVEN owns IS A BOOLEAN, disposed IS A MAYBE DATE, applied IS A DATE, completed IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A `Purchase facts`
`purchase` owns disposed applied completed MEANS `Purchase facts` OF owns, `as a list` disposed, applied, completed, FALSE, FALSE
    WHERE
        `as a list` m MEANS
            CONSIDER m
            WHEN JUST x  THEN LIST x
            WHEN NOTHING THEN EMPTY

GIVEN d IS A Dealing, consent IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Dealing facts`
`dealing` d consent MEANS `Dealing facts` OF d, consent, TRUE

`no re-entry ground` MEANS `Re-entry facts` OF 0, FALSE, FALSE, -1, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE

GIVEN favour IS A NUMBER, total IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Poll result`
`poll` favour total MEANS `Poll result` OF favour, total

§§ `Goal 1 — buying a flat (s 50)`

#ASSERT `entitled to purchase a flat from the Board` (`purchase` FALSE NOTHING (YMD 2026 1 15) NOTHING)
#ASSERT NOT `entitled to purchase a flat from the Board` (`purchase` TRUE NOTHING (YMD 2026 1 15) NOTHING)
-- s 50(1)(b): sold a condominium 30 months before applying — barred; a day earlier — not
#ASSERT NOT `entitled to purchase a flat from the Board` (`purchase` FALSE (JUST (YMD 2023 7 15)) (YMD 2026 1 15) NOTHING)
#ASSERT `entitled to purchase a flat from the Board` (`purchase` FALSE (JUST (YMD 2023 7 14)) (YMD 2026 1 15) NOTHING)
-- a disposal between application and completion is barred too
#ASSERT NOT `entitled to purchase a flat from the Board` (`purchase` FALSE (JUST (YMD 2026 3 1)) (YMD 2026 1 15) (JUST (YMD 2026 6 1)))
#ASSERT `entitled to purchase a flat from the Board` (`purchase` FALSE (JUST (YMD 2026 7 1)) (YMD 2026 1 15) (JUST (YMD 2026 6 1)))
-- s 50(10): exempted
#ASSERT `entitled to purchase a flat from the Board` (`Purchase facts` OF TRUE, EMPTY, (YMD 2026 1 15), NOTHING, TRUE, FALSE)
#ASSERT `the Board may cancel the application on` `(a) a material misrepresentation or false statement`
#ASSERT NOT `the Board may cancel the application on` `none`
-- s 92(1): a DBSS buyer whose spouse is not entitled
#ASSERT NOT `eligible to buy a DBSS flat, person entitled:` TRUE `, spouse entitled:` FALSE `, Minister allows:` FALSE

§§ `Goal 2 — dealings`

-- s 55(3): selling within the minimum occupation period without consent — void
#ASSERT `the effect of` (`dealing` `selling or agreeing to sell within the minimum occupation period` FALSE) EQUALS `void`
#ASSERT `the effect of` (`dealing` `selling or agreeing to sell within the minimum occupation period` TRUE) EQUALS `lawful`
#ASSERT `the effect of` (`dealing` `selling, leasing, mortgaging or otherwise disposing of the flat` FALSE) EQUALS `may be declared void by the Board, and is a breach`
-- s 58(1), (4): a loan from a bank secured on the flat; from a moneylender
#ASSERT `the effect of` (`dealing` (`using the flat or its proceeds as security for a debt` TRUE) FALSE) EQUALS `lawful`
#ASSERT `the effect of` (`dealing` (`using the flat or its proceeds as security for a debt` FALSE) FALSE) EQUALS `void`
#ASSERT `the effect of` (`dealing` `creating a trust of the flat` FALSE) EQUALS `void`
#ASSERT `the effect of` (`dealing` `creating a trust of the flat` TRUE) EQUALS `lawful`
-- s 58(11): no resulting or constructive trust, whatever the Board says
#ASSERT `the effect of` (`dealing` `claiming under a resulting or constructive trust` TRUE) EQUALS `void`
#ASSERT `the effect of` (`dealing` `registering a transmission or transfer on the owner's death` FALSE) EQUALS `cannot be registered without the Board's consent`
-- s 58(6)-(8)
#ASSERT `protected from bankruptcy and attachment, all owners non-citizens:` FALSE `, a consented mortgagee or chargee enforcing:` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `protected from bankruptcy and attachment, all owners non-citizens:` TRUE `, a consented mortgagee or chargee enforcing:` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `protected from bankruptcy and attachment, all owners non-citizens:` FALSE `, a consented mortgagee or chargee enforcing:` TRUE
-- s 59(3): died 1 January 2025; no representation by 1 January 2026
#ASSERT `the Board may vest a deceased owner's flat, died` (YMD 2025 1 1) `, representation` NOTHING `, applied for consent` NOTHING `, consent` NOTHING `, completed` NOTHING `, as at` (YMD 2026 1 1)
#ASSERT NOT `the Board may vest a deceased owner's flat, died` (YMD 2025 1 1) `, representation` NOTHING `, applied for consent` NOTHING `, consent` NOTHING `, completed` NOTHING `, as at` (YMD 2025 12 31)
-- representation 1 March 2025; no application by 1 September 2025 (6 months)
#ASSERT `the Board may vest a deceased owner's flat, died` (YMD 2025 1 1) `, representation` (JUST (YMD 2025 3 1)) `, applied for consent` NOTHING `, consent` NOTHING `, completed` NOTHING `, as at` (YMD 2025 9 2)
#ASSERT NOT `the Board may vest a deceased owner's flat, died` (YMD 2025 1 1) `, representation` (JUST (YMD 2025 3 1)) `, applied for consent` (JUST (YMD 2025 8 1)) `, consent` NOTHING `, completed` NOTHING `, as at` (YMD 2026 9 2)

§§ `Goal 3 — the Board's remedies`

-- s 62(1)(a): 3 months' rent unpaid and a demand by registered post
#ASSERT `the Board may re-enter and determine the lease` (`Re-entry facts` OF 3, TRUE, FALSE, -1, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `the Board may re-enter and determine the lease` (`Re-entry facts` OF 3, FALSE, FALSE, -1, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `the Board may re-enter and determine the lease` (`Re-entry facts` OF 2, TRUE, FALSE, -1, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE)
-- (c): 2 weeks to remedy
#ASSERT NOT `the Board may re-enter and determine the lease` (`Re-entry facts` OF 0, FALSE, FALSE, 14, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE)
#ASSERT `the Board may re-enter and determine the lease` (`Re-entry facts` OF 0, FALSE, FALSE, 15, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `the Board may re-enter and determine the lease` `no re-entry ground`
-- s 63(2): a shophouse worth $250,000 bought with consent for business is no ground; $250,001 is
#ASSERT NOT `a ground for compulsory acquisition` (`(b) owner, spouse or occupier acquired other property` (JUST 250000) NOTHING TRUE)
#ASSERT `a ground for compulsory acquisition` (`(b) owner, spouse or occupier acquired other property` (JUST 250001) NOTHING TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `a ground for compulsory acquisition` (`(b) owner, spouse or occupier acquired other property` (JUST 400000) (JUST 500000) TRUE)
#ASSERT `a ground for compulsory acquisition` (`(b) owner, spouse or occupier acquired other property` NOTHING NOTHING FALSE)
-- (m): above 14 years
#ASSERT NOT `a ground for compulsory acquisition` (`(m) a conviction for throwing things from Board property` 14 TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT `a ground for compulsory acquisition` (`(m) a conviction for throwing things from Board property` 15 TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `a ground for compulsory acquisition` (`(o) repeated abatement or exclusion offences` 0 TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT `the Board may compulsorily acquire the flat on` (LIST `(d) a person other than an authorised occupier resides there`)
#ASSERT NOT `the Board may compulsorily acquire the flat on` EMPTY
#ASSERT `the most financial penalty instead of ss 50, 62 or 63, breach on` (YMD 2015 7 20) EQUALS 50000
#ASSERT `the most financial penalty instead of ss 50, 62 or 63, breach on` (YMD 2015 7 19) EQUALS 0
-- the periods: s 63 notice served 1 March: objection by 29 March; s 66 vesting from 30 March
#ASSERT `the last day to object or appeal for` `s 63 acquisition: objection after notice` `, served` (YMD 2026 3 1) EQUALS YMD 2026 3 29
#ASSERT `the earliest the Board may act on` `s 66 vesting where no objection was made` `, notice served` (YMD 2026 3 1) EQUALS YMD 2026 3 30
#ASSERT `the earliest the Board may act on` `s 50 vesting or termination after notice` `, notice served` (YMD 2026 3 1) EQUALS YMD 2026 3 16
#ASSERT `the earliest the Board may act on` `s 68 taking possession after notice` `, notice served` (YMD 2026 3 1) EQUALS YMD 2026 4 1
#ASSERT `the earliest a varied mortgage rate may apply, notice` (YMD 2026 1 31) EQUALS YMD 2026 2 28
#ASSERT `repair costs must be paid by, notice` (YMD 2026 1 31) `, other date set` NOTHING EQUALS YMD 2026 2 28

§§ `Goal 4 — upgrading`

-- s 77: 75% of the total value in votes
#ASSERT `the poll carries` (`poll` 75 100)
#ASSERT NOT `the poll carries` (`poll` 74.9 100)
#ASSERT `specified upgrading works may be carried out in, general approved:` TRUE `, residential poll` (`poll` 80 100) `, non-residential poll` NOTHING EQUALS `the whole building`
-- s 77(6): residential passes, non-residential fails
#ASSERT `specified upgrading works may be carried out in, general approved:` TRUE `, residential poll` (`poll` 80 100) `, non-residential poll` (JUST (`poll` 50 100)) EQUALS `the residential part only`
#ASSERT `specified upgrading works may be carried out in, general approved:` FALSE `, residential poll` (`poll` 80 100) `, non-residential poll` NOTHING EQUALS `not to be carried out`
#ASSERT `specified upgrading works may be carried out in, general approved:` TRUE `, residential poll` (`poll` 70 100) `, non-residential poll` (JUST (`poll` 90 100)) EQUALS `not to be carried out`
-- s 77(8)(b): combined with general works, the precinct poll must also carry
#ASSERT NOT `special upgrading works may be carried out, building poll` (`poll` 90 100) `, precinct poll if combined` (JUST (`poll` 60 100))
#ASSERT `special upgrading works may be carried out, building poll` (`poll` 90 100) `, precinct poll if combined` NOTHING
#ASSERT `the improvement contribution is due by, demand` (YMD 2026 1 31) EQUALS YMD 2026 2 28
#ASSERT `an unpaid improvement contribution becomes a charge on, demand` (YMD 2026 1 31) EQUALS YMD 2026 4 30
#ASSERT `the earliest the Board may sell the flat, notice of sale` (YMD 2026 5 1) `, sufficient movable property:` FALSE EQUALS JUST (YMD 2026 8 1)
#ASSERT `the earliest the Board may sell the flat, notice of sale` (YMD 2026 5 1) `, sufficient movable property:` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 82(8): $20,000 of proceeds; costs $2,000, contribution $8,000, Town Council $3,000, later mortgage $10,000 — residue 0
#ASSERT `the s 82(8) application of proceeds` 20000 `, claims in order` (LIST 2000, 8000, 3000, 10000) EQUALS LIST 2000, 8000, 3000, 7000, 0
#ASSERT `the s 82(8) application of proceeds` 30000 `, claims in order` (LIST 2000, 8000, 3000, 10000) EQUALS LIST 2000, 8000, 3000, 10000, 7000

